<!--
  The mark: a card with one corner cut away, divided along a line parallel to that cut.

  The two halves are the whole idea. One is filled and one is only outlined, which is the same pairing
  the screen uses for REAL and DISGUISE — one identity present, one merely asserted — and the cut corner
  is the only nod to a SIM. Nothing is drawn twice: the void between the halves is real transparency, so
  the shape survives being tinted for a themed icon or masked down to alpha in the status bar.

  The cut is itself bevelled at both ends, 3 against the card's 6, so the corner reads as machined rather
  than snapped off. Sharp there was the one detail that made the whole mark look unfinished at size.

  The dividing line runs to the opposite corner. Its 45 degrees pass exactly through the centre of that
  corner's radius, which is what makes it read as aimed at the corner rather than merely ending near it,
  and it leaves the void a true half-square: 38 down the left edge, 38 along the bottom.

  Sized to the adaptive-icon safe zone: 38 by 52 of the 108 viewport, centred, putting the far corners
  32.2 from the middle and inside the 66 circle every launcher mask is guaranteed to show.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
